Subject: [PATCH 2/3] =?UTF-8?q?OpenDex:=20OPENDEX=5FRESIZE=20=E2=80=94=20s?=
 =?UTF-8?q?ize=20and=20density=20in=20one=20VirtualDisplay.resize?=
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

New control message type 200 (upstream types 0-22 untouched):
  u8 type | u16 width | u16 height | u16 dpi | u32 bitRate
width = height = 0 keeps the size, dpi = 0 the density, bitRate = 0 the
encoder bit rate (applied by the next patch).

The debounced request carries the density too (newest wins per field), and
triggerResize applies size and density in ONE VirtualDisplay.resize call:
one display configuration change instead of a resize followed by a separate
`wm density`. A density-only request keeps the display's size and, like any
request that does not change the size, adds no pending client-resize entry
to the tracker (no capture reset follows it).
